." Manpage for laptop-welcome
.TH LAPTOP-WELCOME 1 "August 2026" "1.0" "Laptop Welcome Subcommand Manual"
.SH NAME
laptop-welcome \- Show the laptop logo and maintenance status
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B laptop welcome
.SH DESCRIPTION
The welcome subcommand always displays the laptop logo and reports maintenance status for setup, upgrade, and cleanup.
.PP
It warns when setup has not been launched for the current laptop profile version after the configured grace period, when upgrade or cleanup have exceeded their completion interval, or when host uptime reaches the configured threshold (recommending a reboot).
.SH INTERVALS
Intervals are measured in days. Environment variables take precedence over the laptop self configuration file:
.TP
.B LAPTOP_SETUP_DELAY
Grace period after a new profile version is first seen before warning that setup has not been launched. Fallback configuration key: setup_delay. Default: 2 days.
.TP
.B LAPTOP_UPGRADE_DELAY
Fallback configuration key: upgrade_delay. Default: 7 days.
.TP
.B LAPTOP_CLEANUP_DELAY
Fallback configuration key: cleanup_delay. Default: 30 days.
.TP
.B LAPTOP_UPTIME_DELAY
Number of days of host uptime before welcome warns and recommends a reboot. Fallback configuration key: uptime_delay. Default: 30 days.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B laptop welcome
Display the logo and maintenance status.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR laptop (1),
.BR laptop-setup (1),
.BR laptop-upgrade (1),
.BR laptop-cleanup (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by jpolo.
